{{!-- Renders nothing when no app listens on a port. A single repo calls it for its only app (appName). Call it at the top level of a document: hasRootScript reads the context it is called from. --}}
{{#if (listeningApps)}}
{{#if (isMono)}}
An app that listens on a port takes it from the `PORT` environment variable: the commands above run one app on another port from its directory. `PORT` on the root `{{runScript "dev"}}` reaches every app, which then all listen on that port.
{{else}}
The app listens on port {{appPort appName}}. Set `PORT` to listen on another one: `PORT=4000 {{runScript "dev"}}`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (hasRootScript "start")}}
`start` takes `PORT` the same way.
{{/if}}
{{#if (has "tooling" "portless")}}

`dev` and `start:portless` run through portless, which assigns the port itself and ignores `PORT`: set `PORTLESS_APP_PORT` to pin it.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}
